{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And He made my mouth like a sharp sword.</b> For eloquence of speech, or sharp concerning his prophecy concerning Babylon. And the meaning is: even though He made my mouth like a sharp sword, HaShem hid me in the shadow of His hand, and the Babylonians and the wicked of Israel could not prevail against me." "And behold, <b>החביאני</b> is like a sheath for a sword, and the witness is ובאשפתו." "<b>ברור.</b> Pure, bright-looking."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:39.571804410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}